From 7013966cf3680d7e82cbd69f4a799b2de8f24cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:58:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] kebab: XNU-003b drop the 'Reboot to bootloader' menu
 entry

The device shows exactly one BlockIo handle - our own 512 KiB RAM disk
(logical=0 blockSize=512 last=1023) - so there is no storage block device
and the misc partition cannot be reached. kebab.dsc/kebab.fdf contain no
UFS driver at all.

The BootToBl application stays in the tree and still builds (it is a
useful diagnostic and will work once storage is enabled), but it is no
longer packed into the config volume, so the menu returns to:

    Hello Payload / Restart / Power off / Return to firmware

Enabling UFS storage is the prerequisite for xnu-004 anyway.
